# Go build artifacts
/cli/bin/
/cli/dist/
*.test
*.out
coverage.out

# OS
.DS_Store

# Team install output. This repo is where delivery-team's SOURCE lives
# (teams/delivery-team/), and `atl install` writes a byte-identical copy of it
# into .claude/ — ~1.1 MB that would go stale on every team PR and then be
# re-synced at the next release. Same split as .delivery/.gitignore: the source
# files are committed, the derived copy is not. `.delivery/config.json` +
# methodology.json ARE tracked, so a fresh clone still declares its board; the
# ceremonies themselves come back with one `atl install agentteamland/delivery-team`,
# which is also exactly what a user runs — so dogfooding the published team is
# preserved rather than replaced by a repo-local fork. Anything the agents
# accumulate belongs upstream in teams/, never in an installed copy.
/.claude/
/.atl/installed/

# `atl install` scaffolds these unconditionally, but this project is board-backed
# (.delivery/config.json names a backend), and the brainstorm rule is explicit that
# the board is then the single authoritative deferral surface — "one surface only,
# so the two can't drift". Ignored rather than maintained. Tracked as #477.
/.atl/backlog.md
/.atl/tasks.md

# e2e run mirror (stable path for test/e2e/watch.sh)
test/e2e/.last-run.log
# per-lane logs, written beside the aggregate by the lane runner (watch.sh reads them)
test/e2e/.last-run.lane-*.log
